s genuinely easy to answer;\n- read like a human wrote it.\n\nQUALIFICATION RULES\n\nNever write:\n- \"Hi, we are a leading BPO company...\" or any variant that opens with who OptiFlow is;\n- a list of services, or more than one capability;\n- generic compliments: \"love your page\", \"your content is amazing\", \"you guys are crushing it\";\n- fake familiarity: \"I've been following you for a while\", \"I'm a huge fan\";\n- corporate filler: \"I hope this message finds you well\", \"I wanted to reach out\", \"synergy\", \"solutions provider\", \"leverage\", \"streamline your operations\";\n- AI tells: \"In today's fast-paced world\", \"As a business owner, you know\", em-dash-heavy constructions, three-part lists of adjectives;\n- pressure: \"quick call this week?\", \"when are you free?\", \"let me know ASAP\", urgency framing, scarcity framing;\n- more than one emoji across the whole message, and none at all unless the brand's own tone clearly invites it;\n- any claim about their business you cannot support from the input - no invented numbers, no invented customers, no invented reviews;\n- any promise about results, pricing or headcount.\n\nAlways:\n- use their first name only if `address_as` is provided; otherwise open with the observation;\n- use \"you/your\", not \"your company\";\n- keep sentences short. If a sentence runs past about 20 words, split it;\n- ask a question they can answer in one line, about how they currently handle something - not a meeting request;\n- stay under the character limit including spaces;\n- avoid gendered pronouns entirely.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object. No prose, no markdown fence.\n\nJSON SCHEMA\n\n{\n  \"variations\": [\n    { \"variation\": \"conversational\", \"message\": \"...\", \"char_count\": 0 },\n    { \"variation\": \"professional\",   \"message\": \"...\", \"char_count\": 0 },\n    { \"variation\": \"concise\",        \"message\": \"...\", \"char_count\": 0 }\n  ],\n  \"recommended_variation\": \"conversational|professional|concise\",\n  \"recommendation_reason\": \"one sentence on why this variation suits this business\",\n  \"outreach_angle\": \"the angle id used\",\n  \"personalisation_used\": [\"the exact facts you opened with\"],\n  \"self_check\": {\n    \"opens_with_specific_detail\": true|false,\n    \"no_service_list\": true|false,\n    \"ends_with_one_question\": true|false,\n    \"under_max_chars\": true|false,\n    \"no_banned_phrases\": true|false\n  }\n}\n\nSet every self_check field honestly. If any is false, rewrite before responding.\n\nEDGE CASES\n\n- No name available (`address_as` is null): open with the observation. Never write \"Hi there\" or \"Hey!\" alone, and never guess a name.\n- Observations are thin: use the single strongest one and ask a more open question. A short honest message beats a padded one.\n- The business already mentions a support team: acknowledge it and ask about coverage gaps instead of implying they have no support.\n- Medical or dental practice: no claims about patients, outcomes or compliance. Keep it about inquiry handling and admin load.\n- The brand's tone is playful: match it in the conversational variation only. Keep the professional variation neutral.\n- The business posts in another language: write in that language for the conversational variation if you are confident, and note it in recommendation_reason. Otherwise write in English.\n- If the angle and the observations do not support each other, use the observation and note the mismatch in recommendation_reason - the human reviewer decides."
};

const campaign = $('Load Campaign + Niche').first().json;
const niche = campaign.niche || {};
const leads = $('Fetch Lead + Research').all().map((i) => Array.isArray(i.json) ? i.json[0] : i.json);
const out = [];

for (const [index, item] of $input.all().entries()) {
  const research = (Array.isArray(item.json) ? item.json[0] : item.json) || {};
  const row = leads[index] || leads[0];
  if (!row || !row.lead_id) continue;

  const resolved = resolveAngle(niche, research.recommended_angle || row.outreach_angle, {
    lead: { bio: row.bio, products_services: row.products_services },
    research,
    campaign
  });
  const angle = resolved.angle || { id: 'general', label: 'General', hook: 'how they currently handle inbound customer questions' };

  const rendered = renderPrompt(PROMPT, {
    lead: {
      business_name: row.business_name,
      instagram_handle: row.instagram_handle,
      city: row.city,
      state: row.state
    },
    niche,
    decision_maker: {
      address_as: row.decision_maker ? String(row.decision_maker).split(' ')[0] : null,
      contact_role: row.decision_maker_title
    },
    research: {
      business_summary: research.business_summary || row.business_summary || 'No research brief available.',
      what_they_sell: research.what_they_sell,
      instagram_focus: research.instagram_focus,
      specific_observations: research.specific_observations || [],
      operational_pain_points: research.operational_pain_points || [],
      cx_needs: research.cx_needs || [],
      recommended_service: research.recommended_service || row.recommended_service,
      why_optiflow_relevant: research.why_optiflow_relevant || 'Not recorded.'
    },
    angle,
    constraints: { max_chars: campaign.outreach?.max_chars ?? 500 },
    sender: { name: $env.OPTIFLOW_SENDER_NAME || 'Alex', company: 'OptiFlow Solutions' }
  });

  out.push({ json: {
    lead_id: row.lead_id,
    campaign_id: row.campaign_id,
    company_id: row.company_id,
    contact_id: row.contact_id ?? null,
    angle_id: angle.id,
    angle_source: resolved.source,
    max_chars: campaign.outreach?.max_chars ?? 500,
    wanted_variations: campaign.outreach?.variations ?? ['conversational', 'professional', 'concise'],
    default_variation: campaign.outreach?.default_variation ?? 'conversational',
    prompt: rendered.prompt,
    model: campaign.outreach?.model || $env.ANTHROPIC_MODEL_HEAVY || 'claude-opus-5',
    max_tokens: rendered.max_tokens,
    temperature: rendered.temperature,
    prompt_version: rendered.version
